course: dictionary
lesson: 8127
title: A word with a deep meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context shows which one the writer means. «Repentance means turning back: being sorry and changing direction.» The sentence gives you two clues: repentance is being sorry, and it is also changing what you do.
explain: Look at the words around a hard word. In «a sorry repeated every day without change is not real», the words «without change» show that saying sorry is not enough. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: In stories, a word like this often tells you what is happening inside a character, not only what they say. A character who shows repentance has changed how they think, not just what they say.
fact: Repentance is a noun. It means being truly sorry for something wrong and wanting to change.
fact: Saying sorry alone is not always repentance. Real repentance means changing direction, not repeating the same wrong.
fact: In church and the Bible, repentance means turning away from sin and back to God. Christians believe God forgives those who truly repent.
fact: The New Testament word for repentance is «metanoia», which means a change of mind and direction.
fact: John the Baptist called people to repent, and the prodigal son came home in repentance.
exercise: «The New Testament word for repentance, metanoia, means a change of mind and direction.» What does metanoia mean? | A long, quiet walk | A loud argument | *A change of mind and direction | A kind of church music
exercise: Ella says, «Repentance is just saying sorry.» What is missing from her idea? | Being angry with yourself | *Changing direction, not only using words | Nothing, she is right | Forgetting what you did
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Repentance means turning back: being sorry and changing direction.» that shows movement. | being | repentance | *turning | sorry
test: «Christians believe these stories show that God welcomes anyone who turns back (repentance).» In this sentence, who does God welcome? | Nobody at all | *Anyone who turns back | Only people who never do wrong | Only people from their own group
test: The prodigal son came home in repentance. What does this suggest about him? | He was still doing the same wrong | He had forgotten his home | *He had changed inside and was truly sorry | He was angry at his father
exam: Mia says, «Repentance is just saying sorry.» Using the context, what is the best answer? | Repentance means a loud noise | *No, repentance also means changing what you do and turning back | Yes, saying sorry is the whole meaning | No, it means forgetting what happened
